        <owl:annotatedTarget>A membrane-bounded organelle of eukaryotic cells in which chromosomes are housed and replicated. In most cells, the nucleus contains all of the cell&apos;s chromosomes except the organellar chromosomes, and is the site of RNA synthesis and processing. In some species, or in specialized cell types, RNA metabolism or DNA replication may be absent.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GOC:curators</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
