        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0072526"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chemical reactions and pathways resulting in the breakdown of a carbohydrate into pyruvate, with the concomitant production of a small amount of ATP and the reduction of NAD(P) to NAD(P)H. Glycolysis begins with the metabolism of a carbohydrate to generate products that can enter the pathway and ends with the production of pyruvate. Pyruvate may be converted to acetyl-coenzyme A, ethanol, lactate, or other small molecules.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000233 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://github.com/geneontology/go-ontology/issues/21176</obo:IAO_0000233>
        <obo:IAO_0000233 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://github.com/geneontology/go-ontology/issues/30067</obo:IAO_0000233>
