    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0010657">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0006915"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A form of programmed cell death induced by external or internal signals that trigger the activity of proteolytic caspases, whose actions dismantle a muscle cell and result in its death. A muscle cell is a mature contractile cell, commonly known as a myocyte, that forms one of three kinds of muscle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
