        <owl:annotatedTarget>The directed movement of coenzyme A into, out of or within a cell, or between cells, by means of some agent such as a transporter or pore. Coenzyme A, 3&apos;-phosphoadenosine-(5&apos;)diphospho(4&apos;)pantatheine, is an acyl carrier in many acylation and acyl-transfer reactions in which the intermediate is a thiol ester.</owl:annotatedTarget>
