        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chemical reactions and pathways resulting in the formation of any of the vitamin A compounds, retinol, retinal (retinaldehyde) and retinoic acid. Animals cannot synthesize vitamin A de novo, but form it through oxidative cleavage of carotenoids.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/go/patterns/biosynthetic_process.yaml"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>vitamin A anabolism</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
