        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_1901569"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chemical reactions and pathways resulting in the breakdown of ketone bodies, any one of the three substances: acetoacetate, D-3-hydroxybutyrate (beta-hydroxybutyrate) or acetone. Ketone bodies can be used as an energy source as an alternative to glucose. Utilization of ketone bodies in peripheral tissues involves conversion of acetoacetate to acetoacetyl-CoA, which is then converted to two molecules of acetyl-CoA.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/go/patterns/catabolic_process.yaml"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MetaCyc:PWY66-368</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
