            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process in which a relatively unspecialized cell acquires specialized features of a glomerular epithelial cell. Glomerular epithelial cells are specialized epithelial cells that form part of the glomerulus; there are two types, glomerular parietal epithelial cells and glomerular visceral epithelial cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
